<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>

    <title>Simple Quiz</title>

</head>

<body>

<h1>Simple Quiz</h1>

<form id="quizForm">

1. HTML stands for?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q1" value="1"> Hyper Text Markup Language<br>
<input type="radio" name="q1" value="0"> High Text Machine Language<br><br>

2. CSS is used for?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q2" value="1"> Styling<br>
<input type="radio" name="q2" value="0"> Database<br><br>

3. JavaScript is used for?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q3" value="1"> Dynamic Webpages<br>
<input type="radio" name="q3" value="0"> Hardware<br><br>

4. PHP is a?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q4" value="1"> Server-side Language<br>
<input type="radio" name="q4" value="0"> Operating System<br><br>

5. Which tag is used for table row?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q5" value="1"> tr<br>
<input type="radio" name="q5" value="0"> td<br><br>

6. Which symbol is used for id in CSS?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q6" value="1"> #<br>
<input type="radio" name="q6" value="0"> .<br><br>

7. Which function shows popup message?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q7" value="1"> alert()<br>
<input type="radio" name="q7" value="0"> print()<br><br>

8. Which method sends hidden form data?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q8" value="1"> POST<br>
<input type="radio" name="q8" value="0"> GET<br><br>

9. Which tag is used for link?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q9" value="1"> a<br>
<input type="radio" name="q9" value="0"> img<br><br>

10. Which language is used for webpage structure?<br>

<input type="radio" name="q10" value="1"> HTML<br>
<input type="radio" name="q10" value="0"> Python<br><br>

<button type="button" onclick="checkScore()">
    Submit Quiz
</button>

</form>

<h2 id="result"></h2>

<script>

function checkScore(){

    var score = 0;

    for(var i=1; i<=10; i++){

        var ans =
        document.querySelector('input[name="q'+i+'"]:checked');

        if(ans){

            score += parseInt(ans.value);

        }
    }

    document.getElementById("result").innerHTML =
    "Your Score is: " + score + "/10";
}

</script>

</body>

</html>
